      "side": 1,
      "message": "assuming you\u0027re thinking of single bit SET/CLR macros,\nkeep in mind that the macros don\u0027t know the size of the\nbit fields so, i\u0027d prefer to avoid having a single bit\nand a arbitrary-bit version of the accessors unless we\ncan figure out a static assert for the type mismatch.\n\nwhat i\u0027d really like to do here is:\nSET_CO0(EN_LWPWR, enable, reg)\nor\nSET_CO0(EN_LWPWR, !!enable, reg)\ndepending on what we know about the possible values of enable.\n\nif i recall correctly, this is one of the changes\nthat won\u0027t pass compare_builds.sh. i think the change\nis correct, just won\u0027t generate identical instructions.",
